<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibrahim I ibn al-Aghlab</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/756">756</a>–812</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Ibrahim ibn al-Aghlab</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibrahim I ibn al-Aghlab was an Arab army commander who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aghlabid-dynasty">Aghlabid dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a>. In 800 the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harun-al-rashid">Harun al-Rashid</a> made him hereditary governor of the province in return for an annual tribute, giving his family virtual independence. He restored order among the restless Arab troops and built the palace city of al-Abbasiyya near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibrahim-i-ibn-al-aghlab.jpg" alt="Ibrahim I ibn al-Aghlab" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DrFO.Jr.Tn · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aghlabid_dirham_-_Ibrahim_ibn_al-Aghlab_-_al-Maamoun.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 800 the Abbasid caliph Harun al-Rashid appointed <b>Ibrahim I ibn al-Aghlab</b>, the son of a Khurasani Arab commander of the Banu Tamim tribe, hereditary emir of Ifriqiya, in answer to the anarchy that had followed the fall of the Muhallabids in that province.</blockquote><a href="/empire/aghlabid-emirate">Aghlabid emirate · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khorasan</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/turkmenistan">Turkmenistan</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/tunisia">Tunisia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=36,62&amp;year=792" aria-label="Khorasan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6113 864 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Ibrahim I ibn al-Aghlab"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6563 1134h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6563 1134h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=36,62&amp;year=792">What was here in 792 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
